ing plasmonic fields can create a region that acts as a nanoantenna that can enhance the fluorescent emission of a molecule. <jats:bold> Acuna <jats:italic>et al.</jats:italic> </jats:bold> (p. <jats:related-article xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" ext-link-type=\"doi\" page=\"506\" related-article-type=\"in-this-issue\" vol=\"338\" xlink:href=\"10.1126/science.1228638\">506</jats:related-article> ) used a surface-anchored DNA origami structure to assemble one or two gold nanoparticles next to a dye trapped within the structure. A > 100-fold enhancement in fluorescent emission was observed when the dye molecules were located in a 23-nm gap between two 100-nm gold nanoparticles. </jats:p>\n\n## 収録刊行物\n\n  * Science\n    \n\nScience 338 (6106), 506-510, 2012-10-26\n\nAmerican Association for the Advancement of Science (AAAS)\n\n\n## 詳細情報 詳細情報について\n\n  * CRID\n    1360011145399795968\n  * DOI\n    10.1126/science.1228638\n  * ISSN\n    10959203\n    00368075\n  * Web Site\n    https://www.science.org/doi/pdf/10.1126/science.1228638\n\n## 書き出し\n\n  * RefWorksに書き出し\n\n  * EndNoteに書き出し\n\n  * Mendeleyに書き出し\n\n  * RDFで書き出し\n\n  * Refer/BibIXで表示\n\n  * RISで表示\n\n  * BibTeXで表示\n\n  * TSVで表示\n\n  * CSVで表示\n\n  * JSON-LDで表示\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFluorescence Enhancement at Docking Sites of DNA-Directed Self-Assembled Nanoantennas - 科研通 (https://www.ablesci.com/assist/detail?id=DkMJMw)\nciteturn34search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 14.0 years ago; Crawled: last month; 网址  | https://www.science.org/doi/pdf/10.1126/science.1228638\n\n待确认\n\n  * 文献求助详情\n\n标题  | Image: American Association for the Advancement of Science (AAAS) Fluorescence Enhancement at Docking Sites of DNA-Directed Self-Assembled Nanoantennas\n网址  | https://www.science.org/doi/pdf/10.1126/science.1228638\nDOI  | 10.1126/science.1228638 [Button: 复制] doi\n其它  | 期刊：Science\n作者：G. P. Acuna; F. M. Möller; P. Holzmeister; S. Beater; B. Lalkens; e